---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';import Map from '../components/Map.astro';import {places} from '../data/content.json';
---
<Shell title="Places in the Quran"><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">Geography with its sources attached</span> <h1>{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Explore fifteen places the Quran names. Follow the map where the evidence supports a pin, and read the rest without guessing a location.</p></section><section class="panel panel-body"><Map/></section><section class="panel top-gap bottom-gap"><div class="panel-body filters"><label class="field">Find a place<input id="filter" type="search" placeholder="Makkah, Midian, Sinai…"/></label> <label class="field">Location evidence<select id="category"><option value="">All places</option>{[...new Set(places.map(p=>p.kind))].map(k=><option>{k}</option>)}</select></label> <label><input id="saved-only" type="checkbox"/> Saved only</label> <button class="button secondary" id="export">Copy my list</button><span id="count" class="micro" aria-live="polite"></span></div></section><div class="card-grid">{places.map(p=><><article class="panel activity-card" data-item-id={p.id} data-category={p.kind}><span class="eyebrow">{p.kind}</span> <h2><a data-reading-link={p.id} href={`/place/${p.id}/`}>{p.name}</a></h2> <p>{p.summary}</p> <span class="micro">Quran {p.passage.ref}</span> <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`/place/${p.id}/`}>Open place ↗</a> <button class="button secondary" data-save={p.id} aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div></article>{' '}</>)}</div> <div class="empty" id="empty" hidden><h2>Nothing matches</h2> <p>Try another name or change the evidence filter.</p></div><script>import '../lib/library';</script></Shell>
